    lat: 40.0581,
    lng: -82.4013,
    radius: 1400,
    short: "William C. Schenck and others platted Newark in 1802 on the Licking. Named for Newark, New Jersey. County seat. Canal later. The mounds were already here when the plat was drawn.",
