    lat: 41.0442,
    lng: -83.6499,
    radius: 2000,
    short: "Ottawa and Wyandot used the Blanchard. Hull's road north in 1812 came through this country. The fort was a latch on that road. Greenville had opened the paper. The stockade opened the ground.",
